    {
      "context_id": "locked-English-reference:categories:inventory:categories:04SC:lemma/0001:categories-lemma-2-category-fibred-setoids",
      "value": {
        "kind": "locked-English-reference",
        "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14",
        "source_unit": {
          "schema_version": 2,
          "unit_id": "inventory:categories:04SC:lemma/0001",
          "parent_tag": "04S9",
          "chapter": "categories",
          "node_kind": "lemma",
          "risk_level": "R3",
          "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14",
          "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a category. The construction of\nLemma <REF_0001>\npart (2) gives a functor\n<MATHSEG_0001>the 2-category of categories<MATHSEG_0002>fibred in setoids over <MATHSEG_0003>the category of categories<MATHSEG_0004>fibred in sets over <MATHSEG_0005>\n(see\nDefinition <REF_0002>).\nThis functor is an equivalence in the following sense:\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> for any two 1-morphisms <MATH_0002>\nwith <MATH_0003> there exists a unique 2-isomorphism <MATH_0004>,\n<STRUCT_0004> for any morphism <MATH_0005>\nthere exists a 1-morphism <MATH_0006>\nwith <MATH_0007>, and\n<STRUCT_0005> any category fibred in sets <MATH_0008> is equal to <MATH_0009>.\n<STRUCT_0006>\nIn particular, defining <MATH_0010> by the\nrule <MATH_0011>, we have\n<MATHSEG_0006>-isomorphism<MATHSEG_0007>\nMore precisely, given any map <MATH_0012> there exists a\n<MATH_0013>-morphism <MATH_0014> which induces\n<MATH_0015> on isomorphism classes of objects and\nwhich is unique up to unique <MATH_0016>-isomorphism.\n<STRUCT_0007>",
          "source_status": "CURRENT",
          "placeholders": {
            "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{lemma}",
            "LOCKED_0001": "\\label{lemma-2-category-fibred-setoids}",
            "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$",
            "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-setoid-fibres}",
            "MATHSEG_0001": "$$\nF :\n\\left\\{\n\\begin{matrix}\n\\text{",
            "MATHSEG_0002": "}\\\\\n\\text{",
            "MATHSEG_0003": "}\\mathcal{C}\n\\end{matrix}\n\\right\\}\n\\longrightarrow\n\\left\\{\n\\begin{matrix}\n\\text{",
            "MATHSEG_0004": "}\\\\\n\\text{",
            "MATHSEG_0005": "}\\mathcal{C}\n\\end{matrix}\n\\right\\}\n$$",
            "REF_0002": "\\ref{definition-functor-into-2-category}",
            "STRUCT_0002": "\\begin{enumerate}",
            "STRUCT_0003": "\\item",
            "MATH_0002": "$f, g : \\mathcal{S}_1 \\to \\mathcal{S}_2$",
            "MATH_0003": "$F(f) = F(g)$",
            "MATH_0004": "$f \\to g$",
            "STRUCT_0004": "\\item",
            "MATH_0005": "$h : F(\\mathcal{S}_1) \\to F(\\mathcal{S}_2)$",
            "MATH_0006": "$f : \\mathcal{S}_1 \\to \\mathcal{S}_2$",
            "MATH_0007": "$F(f) = h$",
            "STRUCT_0005": "\\item",
            "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{S}$",
            "MATH_0009": "$F(\\mathcal{S})$",
            "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}",
            "MATH_0010": "$F_i \\in \\textit{PSh}(\\mathcal{C})$",
            "MATH_0011": "$F_i(U) = \\Ob(\\mathcal{S}_{i, U})/\\cong$",
            "MATHSEG_0006": "$$\n\\Mor_{\\textit{Cat}/\\mathcal{C}}(\\mathcal{S}_1, \\mathcal{S}_2)\n\\Big/\n2\\text{",
            "MATHSEG_0007": "}\n=\n\\Mor_{\\textit{PSh}(\\mathcal{C})}(F_1, F_2)\n$$",
            "MATH_0012": "$\\phi : F_1 \\to F_2$",
            "MATH_0013": "$1$",
            "MATH_0014": "$f : \\mathcal{S}_1 \\to \\mathcal{S}_2$",
            "MATH_0015": "$\\phi$",
            "MATH_0016": "$2$",
            "STRUCT_0007": "\\end{lemma}"
          },
